    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0806" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.2412 Anti-War/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Kaufman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-10-12T13:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                12</hi>[<hi rendition="#italic">11?</hi>], <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >1928—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 12—10:30
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>46. Bolivia has signed today and delivered to the Legation the multilateral
                    treaty which will be forwarded by pouch.<anchor n="53a" xml:id="d442-f1"/> The
                    President and the Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs Palacios requested my
                    presence at the Palace yesterday afternoon and informed me that <pb facs="0807"
                        n="679" xml:id="pg679"/> Paraguay has violated the mutual understanding in
                    both [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] construction of three forts in disputed
                    territory. Both requested me to notify the Department in the effort to use good
                    influence with Paraguayan Minister in the hope of stopping construction until
                    such time as the matter can be arranged amicably. My answer was that I would
                    convey the foregoing message to the Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaufman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="53a" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>See despatch No. 58, Oct. 12, 1928, from the Chargé in Bolivia, <ref
                        target="#pg220">p. 220</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
